&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Marketing Director&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Chief Commercial Officer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;UK, France, Netherlands, Belgium, Germany, Austria, Spain, Finland, USA. Some travel to our offices will be required from time-to-time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must have the right to work in one the above countries in order to be considered for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💼 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PQShield is looking for a Product Marketing Director who can turn complex technology into stories that people understand, remember, and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own how PQShield&#39;s products, technology, and vision are positioned, communicated, and brought to market worldwide. You&#39;ll sit at the intersection of product, engineering, sales, customers, and the broader security market — translating breakthrough cryptography and security technology into compelling narratives for executives, engineers, partners, and buyers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a strategic product marketer and exceptional storyteller who can identify the market shift, understand the customer problem, and turn complex technology into differentiated positioning that creates urgency, preference and demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since NIST published its first post-quantum cryptography (PQC) standards, which the PQShield team co-authored, organizations across semiconductors, automotive, defense, and enterprise face significant challenges in preparing for the post-quantum transition. This role will help define the market narrative around that transition, position PQShield&#39;s portfolio within it and give customers a clear reason to act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⚒️ What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the story: Develop the narrative, positioning, messaging, and value propositions that explain what is changing in the market, why customers need to act, the problem PQShield solves, and why our approach is differentiated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn technical capability into customer value: Work with cryptographers, engineers and product leaders to understand sophisticated technology, identify what matters to the buyer and translate technical capabilities into clear business and security value without sacrificing technical credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position the portfolio: Own positioning and messaging for our hardware IP and software portfolio, including PQPlatform, PQPerform, PQCryptoLib, and PQMicroLib. Build a clear messaging architecture that connects the portfolio while preserving the differentiated value of each offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the customer: Develop deep insight into customer problems, buying journeys, security requirements, regulatory pressures, barriers to adoption, buying dynamics, and the forces driving post-quantum adoption. Turn those insights into sharper products, messaging, and go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape category and market narrative: Help define how PQShield talks about post-quantum security, cryptographic agility, and the transition to quantum-safe systems — and how we differentiate our approach in a rapidly evolving market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product launches: Create and execute compelling go-to-market strategies for new products, certifications, partnerships, and major releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip the sales team: Build compelling presentations, stories, solution briefs, case studies, battlecards, and other tools that help sales teams communicate value and win complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build buyer and segment-specific stories: Develop differentiated narratives for semiconductors, automotive, military and aerospace, industrial IoT, networking, and enterprise, adapting the value story for different buyers, use cases and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own competitive storytelling: Understand the competitive landscape and turn technical and commercial differences into clear, credible differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create exceptional content: Lead the development of white papers, thought leadership, application notes, customer stories, executive content, web experiences, and other material that establishes PQShield as a category leader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer stories to life: Find and develop the stories that demonstrate why customers are making the transition to post-quantum security and why they choose PQShield.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the company: Partner closely with product, engineering, sales, partnerships, and leadership to ensure the market sees one clear, compelling PQShield story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎯 Required Skills And Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced product marketing leader who is exceptionally strong in positioning, messaging and strategic storytelling. You can take an emerging market, complicated buyer problem or deeply technical product and find the clear narrative inside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of marketing experience, with significant experience in product marketing, technology marketing, B2B marketing, or a closely related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to develop positioning and stories that change how markets understand a product, technology, or company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. You can take something highly technical and make it understandable, interesting, and compelling without dumbing it down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling instincts and the ability to find the human, business, and strategic narrative inside complex technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing technical B2B products, ideally in cybersecurity, semiconductors, infrastructure, embedded systems, software, or another sophisticated technology market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of security and technology buyers, and the ability to communicate credibly with CISOs, CTOs, engineers, architects, product leaders, and business executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work closely with technical experts and quickly develop enough subject-matter expertise to challenge assumptions, ask good questions, and tell an accurate story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commercial mindset: you understand that great marketing isn&#39;t just about explaining a product — it&#39;s about creating differentiation, urgency, preference, and ultimately revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products and taking complex offerings to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing compelling sales narratives and enablement for complex, multi-stakeholder sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent strategic judgment, with the ability to determine what the market needs to hear, why it matters, and how PQShield should say it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment where you will often need to create the narrative before the market has established one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote first company. You will work from home most of the time, but will need to join us in the office for planning sessions and key meetings as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel for customer meetings and marketing events as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and holiday package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions towards 401K/pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;…and other great benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy working as part of a technology company, value the security of our daily digital lives, and love solving hard problems - then we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PQShield is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We’re passionate about talent and proud to foster an inclusive environment; all applicants will be considered regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;PQShield is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We’re passionate about talent and proud to foster an inclusive environment; all applicants will be considered regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role..&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are starting a labour optimisation programme with our Operations team, alongside FP&amp;amp;A and Data Science. The aim is to improve our wage percentage to sales while improving service standards at the same time. We are not interested in an approach that delivers one at the expense of the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently selecting an advanced scheduling platform to support this. The analytical foundation underneath it — how we measure productivity, what our labour standards are, how good our demand forecasts need to be — is what this role owns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will sit in the Data team and work in close partnership with FP&amp;amp;A. Analysis alone will not move the number; changes stick when a Finance Business Partner and a General Manager can see the opportunity in their own House, agree the size of it and hold it in their forecast. Your job is to give them that, in a form they can act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities..&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Labour productivity analysis, identifying site-by-site opportunities for efficiency gains and sizing each one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Operations and Finance to trial changes to scheduling and measure their impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build improved labour reporting, so Business Partners and GMs can see productivity, schedule changes and shift adherence on a daily and weekly cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Finance translate demand forecasts into labour requirements, helping to build the models that turn covers, check-ins, treatments and occupancy into hours by role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our Data Science and Operations teams to understand forecast accuracy and recommend improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect labour deployment to member experience, so that productivity gains are demonstrably not coming out of the House&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Required skills and experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven experience in labour optimisation.&lt;/strong&gt; You have personally delivered measurable improvement in wage percentage or sales per labour hour in a multi-site operation, and can talk us through the levers you pulled, how you sized them and how you proved the result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of partnering finance and operational stakeholders to land change, not just report on it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in an analytics role, with genuine multi-site operational exposure — hospitality, retail, leisure or QSR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL, and comfort in a modelled data warehouse (Snowflake and dbt an advantage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modelling in Excel, and fluency in P&amp;amp;L mechanics — wage percentage, flow-through, contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BI development experience (Omni, Looker, Tableau or Power BI), building tools operators actually use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with rota, time and attendance and payroll data, and a realistic view of its challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to evaluate a demand forecast critically — accuracy, bias, seasonality — without needing to build one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a workforce management or scheduling platform — Unifocus, HotSchedules, Dayforce, Fourth, S4 Labour, UKG, Quinyx or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of how labour regulation constrains labour models internationally, particularly the US — predictive scheduling and fair workweek rules, overtime and break requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Labour standards or time-and-motion experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python for analysis, or use of AI tooling such as Claude Code to accelerate it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience linking labour deployment to customer experience outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure, Inc. (formerly Pure Storage) is adding a Systems (Presales) Engineer to our Commercial district in France, covering the PACA region from Marseille or Aix-en-Provence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a field presales role for someone with 5+ years of hands-on SE experience who enjoys owning a territory. You will partner with several Account Executives across a mixed portfolio: large regional accounts where you drive the technical agenda, public-sector organizations in health, social services and heavy industry, and a long tail of mid-sized companies where speed and pragmatism win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical relationship across your territory: discovery, architecture, demos, proofs of concept and technical closure, on Everpure&#39;s Enterprise Data Cloud platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the initiative in large accounts: build activity, find new use cases, and create opportunities rather than wait for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell outcomes, not boxes: position services and consumption models (Evergreen//One, storage-as-a-service) credibly with IT and finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work day to day with your Account Executives and with channel partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical responses to RFPs and RFIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a national SE team that shares knowledge and wins across districts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING – REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a field presales / Systems Engineer / Solutions Engineer role, ideally with a territory or multi-account scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid general infrastructure culture: compute, virtualisation, networking, data protection, and how they fit together in real customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling services, subscription or consumption models: you can explain the commercial side as well as the technical one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A senior, autonomous way of working: you take initiative, drive activity in large accounts, and manage your own agenda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity: you learn new technology quickly and like finding new use cases for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or near Marseille / Aix-en-Provence, with a driving licence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and professional English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise storage experience (SAN, NAS, object, data protection). Valuable, not required: a dedicated onboarding quarter covers it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background at an infrastructure, data-protection or open-source vendor, or at a services company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with IT teams in the PACA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION &amp;amp; TRAVEL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home-based in the Marseille / Aix-en-Provence area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expect to be with customers around half your time or more. Travel is regional, so you are home in the evening, with occasional trips to Paris for team meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;: We celebrate those who think critically, like a challenge, and aspire to be trailblazers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: We give you the space and support to grow along with us and to contribute to something meaningful. We have been named Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in Technology™, Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™, and certified as a Great Place to Work®!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;: We build each other up and set aside ego for the greater good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And because we understand the value of bringing your full and best self to work, we offer a variety of perks to manage a healthy balance, including flexible time off, wellness resources, and company-sponsored team events. Check out &lt;a href=&quot;http://benefits.everpuredata.com/&quot;&gt;http://benefits.everpuredata.com/ &lt;/a&gt;for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
